{"author":"rebar-bridge[bot]","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1788648775019202002,"compiled_state":{"alias":"relevant-dissident-salamander","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":2,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"72df7654fced731ef470786f29d9167c17d395edb7288f6e06987a276f5a3693","event_uuid":"b1f1020f-773c-4aa0-a0e7-e99fac9c8344","position":{"commit_sha":"bb90de4611e0cea00cea36889dfce10ec9dea2b4","position":"1788648729260632001-b1f1020f-773c-4aa0-a0e7-e99fac9c8344"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"5e0a2ab176e784dfac502b8f8568e44cc63918a59bda2093fcc09b90794302c2","event_uuid":"872527c1-0844-4d49-afe0-a1c8d6868939","position":{"commit_sha":"89364041172f2a6c5fc77aae7c5d7054ad310d6f","position":"1788648775019202001-872527c1-0844-4d49-afe0-a1c8d6868939"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1788648729260632001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"872527c1-0844-4d49-afe0-a1c8d6868939","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"5bba-45dd-3bfc-42f1"}],"description":"## Summary\n\nThe Gerrit host `i-00880b2c7f13527c5` is a **burstable `t4g.large`** (2 vCPU / 7.8 GiB) whose\n**CPU credit balance has been exhausted since 12:38 UTC on 2026-09-05** and has stayed at zero.\nIt is now running entirely on billed surplus credits, which are accruing. This is a structural\ninstance-sizing and cost finding, distinct from the proxy-timeout defect it was discovered under.\n\nDiscovered while root-causing `antihuman-beefwitted-zebra` (`5bba-45dd-3bfc-42f1`). Raising the\nnginx read timeout stops the 504s; it does **not** address this. The host remains short of CPU.\n\n## Measurements (CloudWatch, `AWS/EC2`, instance `i-00880b2c7f13527c5`, 1h Average)\n\n**`CPUCreditBalance`** — steady decline through 2026-09-04, hits zero and stays there:\n\n```\n2026-09-04 15:38 PT  352.9      2026-09-05 02:38 PT   74.9\n2026-09-04 18:38 PT  281.1      2026-09-05 03:38 PT   31.6\n2026-09-04 21:38 PT  166.2      2026-09-05 04:38 PT   13.7\n2026-09-05 01:38 PT  116.3      2026-09-05 05:38 PT    0.0   <- exhausted (12:38 UTC)\n                                2026-09-05 06:38..14:38 PT  0.0  (10 further hours at zero)\n```\n\n**`CPUSurplusCreditBalance`** — climbing continuously since exhaustion, i.e. accruing charges:\n\n```\n05:38 PT  15.5    07:38 PT  40.7    09:38 PT 117.0    11:38 PT 206.0    13:38 PT 281.1\n06:38 PT  20.1    08:38 PT  78.9    10:38 PT 168.3    12:38 PT 254.4    14:38 PT 316.7\n```\n\n**`CPUUtilization`** — sustained **55-74%** across the day against a **30% baseline** for\n`t4g.large`. The instance is in `unlimited` mode (`describe-instance-credit-specifications`\nreturns `unlimited`), so it is not hard-throttled yet, but it is running roughly 2x its\nentitlement continuously and paying for the difference.\n\n**On-host corroboration:**\n\n- `vmstat` showed CPU `steal` reaching **13%**.\n- Load average **9-12 on 2 vCPU** (`/proc/loadavg`: `9.49 9.04 9.81`, later `12.61 11.33 10.55`).\n- Gerrit `git-upload-pack` requests spend only **~24% of wall time on CPU** (median over 37\n  anonymous CI fetches from `/var/gerrit/logs/httpd_log`) — off-CPU ~76% of the time. A full\n  clone needs ~20-28s of CPU and takes 85-144s of wall.\n- Memory: `free -m` showed 202 MB free of 7813, **no swap**, `kswapd0` active, page cache\n  squeezed to ~600-714 MB on a git server.\n\n**Correlation with the 504 incidents:** all four `Gerrit Verified Gate` checkout failures on\n2026-09-05 (15:38, 15:39, 21:52, 22:08 UTC) occurred **after** the credit balance hit zero at\n12:38 UTC. The earlier cluster (02:51-03:08 UTC) occurred while the balance was collapsing\n(74.9 -> 31.6 -> 13.7).\n\n## Largest single consumer — and what is NOT established about it\n\n`ps` on the host: **`rebar-mcp` at 4.45 GB RSS (55.6% of RAM) and 47% CPU**, against Gerrit's JVM\nat 765 MB RSS / 3.3% and the review-bot at 746 MB / 4.1%.\n\n**NOT ESTABLISHED:** that `rebar-mcp`'s footprint *causes* the credit exhaustion. It is the\nlargest consumer by a wide margin, which is correlation. It has not been shown to be a leak rather\nthan steady state, and no measurement attributes a share of credit burn to it.\n\n**Re-measure before acting on that number.** Change **2685** merged tonight — a per-ticket\nprojection in `reduce_all_tickets`, measured to cut whole-store read cost from ~295 MB to ~84 MB\nper concurrent call. **It has not been deployed to the host**, so the 4.45 GB above predates it.\nWhoever picks this up should take a fresh reading after that deploy rather than inheriting this\nfigure.\n\n## Why this is worth its own ticket\n\nRaising the nginx `proxy_read_timeout` (bug `5bba`) stops the 504s by no longer converting slow-\nbut-successful responses into errors. It leaves untouched the reason those responses are slow. A\nhost at zero credits with sustained 2x-baseline utilisation will keep degrading every latency-\nsensitive surface on it — Gerrit git serving, the review-bot's voting (`voter_errors`), the MCP\nservice, the observability probe — and will keep costing surplus charges.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1 A fresh `CPUCreditBalance` / `CPUSurplusCreditBalance` / `CPUUtilization` reading is\n      taken AFTER change 2685 is deployed, so the decision rests on current data.\n- [ ] AC2 The credit burn is attributed across tenants (Gerrit JVM, rebar-mcp, review-bot,\n      opcert, autodeploy, observability) rather than assumed, so the remedy targets the actual\n      consumer.\n- [ ] AC3 A decision is recorded between the available remedies, with its cost basis: move to a\n      non-burstable instance class, resize, reduce tenancy (move build/gate work off the Gerrit\n      host), or accept `unlimited` surplus charges as the steady state.\n- [ ] AC4 If `unlimited` surplus is accepted, an alarm exists on `CPUSurplusCreditBalance` so the\n      charge is observed rather than discovered on a bill.\n- [ ] AC5 Whether `rebar-mcp`'s RSS is a leak or steady state is settled by measurement.\n\n## Constraints\n\nProduction is read-only for investigation; instance-class changes are operator-authorized and must\nfollow a reviewed plan. Never use `--force` or any gate bypass.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"9892-fff8-1f3b-4759","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Gerrit host t4g.large has run at zero CPU credits since 12:38Z, on billed surplus, at sustained 2x its baseline","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["b1f1020f-773c-4aa0-a0e7-e99fac9c8344","872527c1-0844-4d49-afe0-a1c8d6868939"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788648775019202002,"uuid":"7276707e-1611-46ef-b898-e98eaeb7b38b"}